IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`
IMPORT `ucta-p1-avoidance`
IMPORT `ucta-fixtures`
IMPORT `ucta-part3`
IMPORT `ucta-p1-introductory`

-- Tests for ucta-p1-avoidance.l4 (sections 2 to 4).  Every expected value is written from the text.
-- The last argument of each section function is the reach of the section, computed in ucta-p1-introductory
-- and tested there; here it is given.


§ `s 2(1)`

-- "A person cannot ... exclude or restrict his liability for death or personal injury resulting from negligence".
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for death or personal injury resulting from negligence` `Death or personal injury` TRUE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The First Schedule or section 1(3) takes the section out of the case: the bar does not apply and nothing is granted.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for death or personal injury resulting from negligence` `Death or personal injury` TRUE `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for death or personal injury resulting from negligence` `Death or personal injury` TRUE `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Other loss or damage is subsection (2).
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for death or personal injury resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not resulting from negligence.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for death or personal injury resulting from negligence` `Death or personal injury` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 2(2)`

#ASSERT `s 2(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the term or notice` `Other loss or damage` TRUE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Death or personal injury is subsection (1), which has no reasonableness exception.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the term or notice` `Death or personal injury` TRUE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the term or notice` `Other loss or damage` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the term or notice` `Other loss or damage` TRUE `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the term or notice` `Other loss or damage` TRUE `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "cannot so exclude or restrict ... except in so far as the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness": it does not.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The term is reasonable: the bar is lifted and nothing is granted (ruling QA, by the text's spelling).
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Reasonableness is not shown by anyone: it is for those claiming it to show it (s 11(5)), so the bar stands.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Death or personal injury` TRUE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE (JUST FALSE) `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE (JUST FALSE) `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 2(3)`

-- "is not of itself to be taken as indicating his voluntary acceptance of any risk".
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person's agreement to or awareness of the term or notice is of itself to be taken as indicating voluntary acceptance of the risk` TRUE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person's agreement to or awareness of the term or notice is of itself to be taken as indicating voluntary acceptance of the risk` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person's agreement to or awareness of the term or notice is of itself to be taken as indicating voluntary acceptance of the risk` TRUE `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person's agreement to or awareness of the term or notice is of itself to be taken as indicating voluntary acceptance of the risk` TRUE `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 3(1)`

-- One of them deals as consumer.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this section applies as between the contracting parties` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One of them deals on the other's written standard terms of business.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this section applies as between the contracting parties` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this section applies as between the contracting parties` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither limb: the "where" is not met.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this section applies as between the contracting parties` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Consumer status unknown, but standard terms settle it.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this section applies as between the contracting parties` TRUE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Consumer status unknown and no standard terms: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this section applies as between the contracting parties` TRUE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not contracting parties.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this section applies as between the contracting parties` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this section applies as between the contracting parties` FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 3(2)`

-- (a): the person is himself in breach and excludes liability for the breach.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Excludes or restricts the other party's liability for its own breach of contract` TRUE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) speaks of the person "when himself in breach of contract".
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Excludes or restricts the other party's liability for its own breach of contract` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(i): the person's own breach is not needed.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Something else` TRUE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 3 does not apply as between these parties.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` NOTHING `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A notice having contractual effect is neither a contract term nor a notice not having contractual effect (fork).
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A notice that has contractual effect` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 3(2) speaks of "any contract term".
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A notice that does not have contractual effect` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The term is within (b)(i) and is not reasonable.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Excludes or restricts the other party's liability for its own breach of contract` TRUE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reasonable: the bar is lifted and nothing is granted (ruling QA).
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Reasonableness is not shown by anyone: it is for those claiming it to show it (s 11(5)), so the bar stands.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside (a): the person is not in breach.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Excludes or restricts the other party's liability for its own breach of contract` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Something else` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST FALSE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A notice that does not have contractual effect` `Claims a right to render a contractual performance substantially different from that reasonably expected` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 4(1)`

#ASSERT `s 4(1) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a person dealing as consumer: section 4(1) says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` NOTHING TRUE `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- No indemnity for another's liability.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) FALSE `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A notice that does not have contractual effect` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A notice that has contractual effect` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A contract term` `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "cannot ... be made to indemnify ... except in so far as the contract term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness": it does not.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person dealing as consumer can be made to indemnify the other person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reasonable: the bar is lifted and nothing is granted (ruling QA).
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person dealing as consumer can be made to indemnify the other person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Reasonableness is not shown by anyone: it is for those claiming it to show it (s 11(5)), so the bar stands.
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person dealing as consumer can be made to indemnify the other person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A contract term` NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person dealing as consumer can be made to indemnify the other person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person dealing as consumer can be made to indemnify the other person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person dealing as consumer can be made to indemnify the other person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 4(2)`

#ASSERT `s 4(2) section 4 applies to the liability` `Directly by the person to be indemnified` `To the person dealing as consumer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) section 4 applies to the liability` `Directly by the person to be indemnified` `To someone else` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) section 4 applies to the liability` `Vicariously by the person to be indemnified` `To the person dealing as consumer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) section 4 applies to the liability` `Vicariously by the person to be indemnified` `To someone else` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) section 4 applies to the liability` `In another way` `To someone else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Item 1 of the fix round: a flat negative takes the section out of the case`

-- The twin ("a requirement of reasonableness applies") is in the text's own polarity, so the text's own no is JUST FALSE.
-- It comes before the scope limits: the section does not extend to the contract at all.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the term or notice` `Death or personal injury` TRUE `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the term or notice` `Other loss or damage` FALSE `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `A contract term` `Something else` FALSE `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) FALSE `A notice that does not have contractual effect` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where the reach cannot be told, the twin stays NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `A contract term` `Something else` FALSE `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The functions that ask whether the person CAN exclude or rely stay NOTHING when the section is out: the Act then says nothing about whether they can.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE (JUST FALSE) `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE (JUST FALSE) `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING

-- End to end, through the section 1(2) aggregator.  An insurance policy's no-performance term under section 3:
-- First Schedule paragraph 1(a) says sections 2 to 4 do not extend to any contract of insurance.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE (`s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 3` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `Insurance, including a contract to pay an annuity on human life` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) (`s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` `an ordinary part 3`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The other side: the same term in a contract that touches nothing in the Schedule, with the same facts.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE (`s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 3` (`an ordinary scope`) (`s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` `an ordinary part 3`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Section 1(3): the liability is not business liability, and sections 2 to 7 apply "only to business liability".
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE (`s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 3` (`mk scope` FALSE `Another kind of contract` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) (`s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` `an ordinary part 3`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Part 3, section 26(2): an international supply contract is not subject to a requirement of reasonableness under section 3 or 4.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE (`s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 3` (`mk scope` TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` `None of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) (`s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `A contract of sale of goods` (`mk part3` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)))) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Employment: section 2(1) and (2) "do not extend to a contract of employment, except in favour of the employee".
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the term or notice` `Other loss or damage` TRUE (`s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 2(2)` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `Employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) (`s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` `an ordinary part 3`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ... except in favour of the employee: the bar is lifted for the employee, so the section is not out of the case.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the term or notice` `Other loss or damage` TRUE (`s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 2(2)` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `Employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE) (`s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` `an ordinary part 3`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Removal that rests on something the text does not settle stays NOTHING: whether the person protected deals as consumer is not known, and paragraph 2 (marine salvage or towage) answers differently on either answer.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE (`s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 3` (`mk scope` TRUE `Another kind of contract` `Marine salvage or towage` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE) (`s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` `an ordinary part 3`)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Part 3 that turns on the Minister's order (outside the text) stays NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE (`s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the section out of the case` `Section 3` (`an ordinary scope`) (`s 1(2) whether Part 3 takes sections 2 to 7 out of the case` `Another kind of contract` (`mk part3` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE `Something else` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2024) (Date 1 3 2024) (JUST FALSE)))) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Item 3 of the fix round: reasonableness nobody has shown (s 11(5))`

-- It is for those claiming that the term satisfies the requirement to show that it does.  Not shown (JUST FALSE or NOTHING): the bar stands, JUST FALSE.
-- Shown: the bar is lifted and nothing is granted (ruling QA); the answer stays NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Other loss or damage` TRUE (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Claims a right to render no performance at all, in respect of the whole or part of the obligation` FALSE (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person dealing as consumer can be made to indemnify the other person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A contract term` NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person dealing as consumer can be made to indemnify the other person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Outside the zone (no requirement applies) the answer does not depend on reasonableness.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the person can exclude or restrict liability for other loss or damage resulting from negligence` `Death or personal injury` TRUE NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the other party can rely on the contract term as against that party` (JUST TRUE) `A contract term` `Something else` FALSE NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Item 2 of the fix round: s 2(3) in its own words`

-- "Where a contract term or notice purports to exclude or restrict liability for negligence, a person's agreement to or awareness of it is not of itself to be taken as indicating his voluntary acceptance of any risk".
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person's agreement to or awareness of the term or notice is not of itself to be taken as indicating voluntary acceptance of the risk` TRUE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The "Where" is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person's agreement to or awareness of the term or notice is not of itself to be taken as indicating voluntary acceptance of the risk` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person's agreement to or awareness of the term or notice is not of itself to be taken as indicating voluntary acceptance of the risk` TRUE `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person's agreement to or awareness of the term or notice is not of itself to be taken as indicating voluntary acceptance of the risk` TRUE `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The positive question stays NOTHING outside the "Where": the subsection does not say that agreement IS acceptance.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person's agreement to or awareness of the term or notice is of itself to be taken as indicating voluntary acceptance of the risk` FALSE `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
